            "review_title": "Review at MÌ CÁ HONGKONG 1988 - CN TRẦN NÃO",
            "review_text": "Global62529396667\n5 contributions\n0\nHong Kong is beautiful and cosy!\nJun 2026 • Friends\nI just visited the newly opened branch experience of Miy Hong Kong Fish 1988 at No. 65 Chan Brain and was really pleased. The wine here is extremely delicious, the water is thick and Hong Kong standard.\n\nThe space is spacious, cool, giving a very pleasant feeling. Besides good food, what impresses me most is the cozy, intimate atmosphere that the restaurant brings — just like an ideal place for families or loved ones to sit together and share a hot breakfast before the start of the new day. Both the food and the service made me happy. I will definitely come back many times!\n\nI recently visited the newly opened branch of Mi Ca Hong Kong 1988 at 65 Tran Nao, and it was a wonderful experience! The noodles here are absolutely delicious and capture the authentic taste of Hong Kong.\n\nThe restaurant has a spacious, airy, and very comfortable atmosphere. What I love most about this place, besides the great food, is the warm and family-friendly vibe they cultivate. It’s the perfect spot to enjoy a cozy, hearty breakfast with your loved ones before starting the day. I am completely satisfied with both the food and the service. Highly recommended for anyone looking for great noodles in District 2!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten June 25, 2026",
